<p style="text-align: left;">Which of the following describes function <math alttext="f"><mi>f</mi>
</math>?</p>$SATQ$, $SATQ$[{"id":"76efc54f-b6a1-4d87-a00d-7afb9d20c619","content":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Increasing linear</p>"},{"id":"73b2204c-3f51-4c58-9e2f-f55268b15a85","content":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Decreasing linear</p>"},{"id":"b608823b-4a94-4c9c-81f9-e2ba31c5e92b","content":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Increasing exponential</p>"},{"id":"e55345f1-0cef-49e2-a201-e36780e58dab","content":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Decreasing exponential</p>"}]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["A"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["76efc54f-b6a1-4d87-a00d-7afb9d20c619"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$<p style="text-align: left;">Choice A is correct. The graph of function <math alttext="f"><mi>f</mi>
</math> shows that as <math alttext="x"><mi>x</mi>
</math> increases, <math alttext="f left parenthesis x right parenthesis"><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced></math> also increases, which means <math alttext="f left parenthesis x right parenthesis"><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced></math> is an increasing function. The graph of <math alttext="f"><mi>f</mi>
</math> is a line, which indicates a constant rate of change. A function that has a constant rate of change is a linear function. Therefore, function <math alttext="f"><mi>f</mi>
</math> can be described as increasing linear.</p>
<p style="text-align: left;">Choice B is incorrect. For a decreasing function, as <math alttext="x"><mi>x</mi>
</math> increases, <math alttext="f left parenthesis x right parenthesis"><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced></math> decreases, rather than increases.</p>
<p style="text-align: left;">Choice C is incorrect. The graph of an exponential function isn't a line.</p>
<p style="text-align: left;">Choice D is incorrect. For a decreasing function, as&nbsp;<math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="x"><mi>x</mi></math> increases,&nbsp;<math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="f left parenthesis x right parenthesis"><mi>f</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>)</mo></math> decreases, rather than increases, and the graph of an exponential function isn't a line.</p>$SATQ$, false, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, $SATQ${"questionId":"c141366d","external_id":"f8342a9a-48d1-4fe3-865b-171f9d9f8f72","disclosed_item_id":null,"source":"qbank","vaultid":null,"uId":"ab28a2cb-0fc5-4bf4-82ea-385b415d6e91","program":"SAT","test_type":2,"test_type_desc":"Math","primary_class_cd":"Q","domain":"Problem-Solving and Data Analysis","skill_cd":"Q.D.","skill_desc":"Two-variable data: Models and scatterplots","difficulty":"E","score_band_range_cd":2,"type":"mcq","stimulus":null,"stem":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">The graph of function <math alttext=\"f\"><mi>f</mi>\n</math> is shown, where <math alttext=\"y equals f left parenthesis x right parenthesis\"><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced></math>.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><figure class='image'><svg height=\"275.22pt\" version=\"1.1\" viewBox=\"0 0 288.918319 275.22\" width=\"288.918319pt\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Graph of a line in the x y plane with the origin labeled O. The x axis ranges from negative 10 to 10. The y axis ranges from negative 10 to 10. Refer to long description.\">\n <defs>\n  <style type=\"text/css\">\n*{stroke-linecap:butt;stroke-linejoin:round;}\n  </style>\n </defs>\n <g id=\"figure_1\">\n  <g id=\"patch_1\">\n   <path d=\"M 0 275.22 \nL 288.918319 275.22 \nL 288.918319 0 \nL 0 0 \nz\n\" style=\"fill:none;\"></path>\n  </g>\n  <g id=\"axes_1\">\n   <g id=\"patch_2\">\n    <path d=\"M 9.558319 260.46 \nL 281.718319 260.46 \n