</math> eggs is added to create a new data set. Which of the following correctly compares the means of the two data sets?</p>$SATQ$, $SATQ$[{"id":"ecc4bff6-0a8e-4214-86be-3a91ad7376fc","content":"<p>The mean of the original data set is greater than the mean of the new data set.</p>"},{"id":"0ea27478-5476-4147-9f58-a60448733eb8","content":"<p>The mean of the original data set is less than the mean of the new data set.</p>"},{"id":"62584586-78a7-410d-ba31-f9c138954bc2","content":"<p>The means of both data sets are equal.</p>"},{"id":"e3da55f3-369e-4ef5-b992-7c9440ce3870","content":"<p>There is not enough information to compare the means.</p>"}]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["A"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["ecc4bff6-0a8e-4214-86be-3a91ad7376fc"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$<p style="text-align: left;">Choice A is correct. It's given that the table shows an original data set of <math alttext="5"><mn>5</mn>
