    ($SATQ$c47256ca$SATQ$, $SATQ$d6f8cc02-96fe-42b9-bfb6-5bd07411ccfc$SATQ$::uuid, NULL, NULL, $SATQ$qbank$SATQ$, $SATQ$SAT$SATQ$, 2, $SATQ$Math$SATQ$, $SATQ$Problem-Solving and Data Analysis$SATQ$, $SATQ$Q$SATQ$, $SATQ$Q.A.$SATQ$, $SATQ$Ratios, rates, proportional relationships, and units$SATQ$, $SATQ$E$SATQ$, 1, $SATQ$mcq$SATQ$, NULL, $SATQ$<p>An object's speed is <math alttext="64 yards"><mrow><mn>64</mn></mrow><mo>&#160;</mo><mtext>yards</mtext></math> per second. What is the object's speed, in <span style="text-decoration: underline;">feet</span> per second? <math alttext="left parenthesis 1 yard  equals 3 feet right parenthesis"><mfenced><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mtext>yard</mtext><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mtext>feet</mtext></mrow></mfenced></math></p>$SATQ$, $SATQ$[{"id":"949912ef-296c-4c13-aeeb-6f4d9d2dca4c","content":"<p><math alttext=\"61\"><mn>61</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"2d3c93cc-e13c-482e-84d7-4e705ac7d1ab","content":"<p><math alttext=\"67\"><mn>67</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"a6c2a6ad-3cb9-47b8-a401-d8151818909d","content":"<p><math alttext=\"94\"><mn>94</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"e4278050-8890-4687-9d8b-09bf3bda8ddf","content":"<p><math alttext=\"192\"><mn>192</mn>\n</math></p>"}]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["D"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["e4278050-8890-4687-9d8b-09bf3bda8ddf"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$<p style="text-align: left;">Choice D is correct. Since <math alttext="1"><mn>1</mn>
</math> yard is equal to <math alttext="3"><mn>3</mn>
</math> feet, <math alttext="64"><mn>64</mn>
</math> yards is equal to <math alttext="64 yards left parenthesis StartFraction 3 feet Over 1 yard EndFraction right parenthesis"><mn>64</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mtext>yards</mtext><mfenced><mfrac><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mtext>feet</mtext></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mtext>yard</mtext></mrow></mfrac></mfenced></math>, or <math alttext="192"><mn>192</mn>
</math> feet. It follows that <math alttext="64"><mn>64</mn>
</math> yards per second is equivalent to <math alttext="192"><mn>192</mn>
</math> feet per second. Therefore, the object's speed is <math alttext="192"><mn>192</mn>
</math> feet per second.</p>
<p style="text-align: left;">Choice A is incorrect. A speed of <math alttext="61"><mn>61</mn>
</math> feet per second is equivalent to&nbsp;<math alttext="StartFraction 61 Over 3 EndFraction"><mfrac><mn>61</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac></math>, not <math alttext="64"><mn>64</mn>
</math>, yards per second.</p>
<p style="text-align: left;">Choice B is incorrect. A speed of <math alttext="67"><mn>67</mn>
</math> feet per second is equivalent to&nbsp;<math alttext="StartFraction 67 Over 3 EndFraction"><mfrac><mn>67</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac></math>, not <math alttext="64"><mn>64</mn>
</math>, yards per second.</p>
<p style="text-align: left;">Choice C is incorrect. A speed of <math alttext="94"><mn>94</mn>
</math> feet per second is equivalent to&nbsp;<math alttext="StartFraction 94 Over 3 EndFraction"><mfrac><mn>94</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac></math>, not <math alttext="64"><mn>64</mn>
</math>, yards per second.</p>$SATQ$, false, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, $SATQ${"questionId":"c47256ca","external_id":"d6f8cc02-96fe-42b9-bfb6-5bd07411ccfc","disclosed_item_id":null,"source":"qbank","vaultid":null,"uId":"b418310a-f5f4-4696-87da-938d4d47f2e4","program":"SAT","test_type":2,"test_type_desc":"Math","primary_class_cd":"Q","domain":"Problem-Solving and Data Analysis","skill_cd":"Q.A.","skill_desc":"Ratios, rates, proportional relationships, and units","difficulty":"E","score_band_range_cd":1,"type":"mcq","stimulus":null,"stem":"<p>An object's speed is <math alttext=\"64 yards\"><mrow><mn>64</mn></mrow><mo>&#160;</mo><mtext>yards</mtext></math> per second. What is the object's speed, in <span style=\"text-decoration: underline;\">feet</span> per second? <math alttext=\"left parenthesis 1 yard  equals 3 feet right parenthesis\"><mfenced><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mtext>yard</mtext><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mtext>feet</mtext></mrow></mfenced></math></p>","answerOptions":[{"id":"949912ef-296c-4c13-aeeb-6f4d9d2dca4c","content":"<p><math alttext=\"61\"><mn>61</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"2d3c93cc-e13c-482e-84d7-4e705ac7d1ab","content":"<p><math alttext=\"67\"><mn>67</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"a6c2a6ad-3cb9-47b8-a401-d8151818909d","content":"<p><math alttext=\"94\"><mn>94</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"e4278050-8890-4687-9d8b-09bf3bda8ddf","content":"<p><math alttext=\"192\"><mn>192</mn>\n</math></p>"}],"keys":["e4278050-8890-4687-9d8b-09bf3bda8ddf"],"correct_answer":["D"],"rationale":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice D is correct. Since <math alttext=\"1\"><mn>1</mn>\n</math> yard is equal to <math alttext=\"3\"><mn>3</mn>\n</math> feet, <math alttext=\"64\"><mn>64</mn>\n</math> yards is equal to <math alttext=\"64 yards left parenthesis StartFraction 3 feet Over 1 yard EndFraction right parenthesis\"><mn>64</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mtext>yards</mtext><mfenced><mfrac><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mtext>feet</mtext></mrow><mrow>