$SATQ$, $SATQ$<p class="stem_paragraph ">What is the range of the number of wheels made for the 11&nbsp;one-hour periods?</p>
$SATQ$, $SATQ$[{"id":"a","content":"<p>5.5</p>\n"},{"id":"b","content":"<p>5.0</p>\n"},{"id":"c","content":"<p>4.5</p>\n"},{"id":"d","content":"<p>4.0</p>\n"}]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["B"]$SATQ$::jsonb, NULL, $SATQ$<p>Choice B is correct. Range is defined as the difference between the greatest and least values from a set of data. The greatest number of wheels made during a one-hour period was 24 wheels. The least number of wheels was 19. Hence, the range is <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/c54b92a2/img_000_d15ba732.png" alt="24 minus 19, equals 5"></span>, or 5.0.<p>Choices A, C, and D are incorrect and may be the result of arithmetic errors or incorrectly identifying the greatest or least number of wheels made during a one-hour period.</p></p>
