<div role="region" aria-label="Long description for scatterplot" class="sr-only"><ul><li>The scatterplot has 6 data points.</li>
<li>The data points are in a linear pattern trending up from left to right.</li>
<li>A line of best fit is shown:
<ul>
<li>The line of best fit slants up from left to right.</li>
<li>The line of best fit passes through the following approximate coordinates:<br>
<ul>
<li>(0 comma 3.4)</li>
<li>(8 comma 11)</li>
<li>(12 comma 14.8)</li>
</ul>
</li>
</ul>
</li>
</ul></div></figure></p>
<p style="text-align: left;">Which of the following equations best represents the line of best fit shown?</p>$SATQ$, $SATQ$[{"id":"4ed230fa-e065-42ee-aacb-9a7b0ad6a7df","content":"<p><math alttext=\"y equals x plus 3.4\"><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>3.4</mn></mrow></math></p>"},{"id":"0ad0547b-914a-410e-aeb5-1ae2be64bdb8","content":"<p><math alttext=\"y equals x minus 3.4\"><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mrow><mn>3.4</mn></mrow></math></p>"},{"id":"18b90c4e-3d0d-4a9d-b74e-54017be1e356","content":"<p><math alttext=\"y equals negative x plus 3.4\"><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>3.4</mn></mrow></math></p>"},{"id":"efcd9781-bbe9-4dc9-8490-aa4b28ffd99c","content":"<p><math alttext=\"y equals negative x minus 3.4\"><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mrow><mn>3.4</mn></mrow></math></p>"}]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["A"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["4ed230fa-e065-42ee-aacb-9a7b0ad6a7df"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$<p style="text-align: left;">Choice A is correct. The line of best fit shown has a positive slope and intersects the <em>y</em>-axis at a positive <em>y</em>-value. The graph of an equation of the form <math alttext="y equals m x plus b"><mrow>
<mi>y</mi>
<mo>=</mo>
<mrow>
<mrow>
<mi>m</mi>
<mi>x</mi>
</mrow>
<mo>+</mo>
<mi>b</mi>
</mrow>
</mrow>
</math>, where <math alttext="m"><mi>m</mi>
</math> and <math alttext="b"><mi>b</mi>
</math> are constants, has a slope of <math alttext="m"><mi>m</mi>
</math> and intersects the <em>y</em>-axis at a <em>y</em>-value of <math alttext="b"><mi>b</mi>
</math>. Of the given choices, only <math alttext="y equals x plus 3.4"><mrow>
<mi>y</mi>
<mo>=</mo>
<mrow>
<mi>x</mi>
<mo>+</mo>
<mn>3.4</mn>
</mrow>
</mrow>
</math> represents a line that has a positive slope, <math alttext="1"><mn>1</mn>
</math>, and intersects the <em>y</em>-axis at a positive <em>y</em>-value, <math alttext="3.4"><mn>3.4</mn>
</math>.</p>
<p style="text-align: left;">Choice B is incorrect. This equation represents a line that intersects the <em>y</em>-axis at a negative <em>y</em>-value, not a positive <em>y</em>-value.</p>
<p style="text-align: left;">Choice C is incorrect. This equation represents a line that has a negative slope, not a positive slope.</p>
<p style="text-align: left;">Choice D is incorrect. This equation represents a line that has a negative slope, not a positive slope, and intersects the <em>y</em>-axis at a negative <em>y</em>-value, not a positive <em>y</em>-value.</p>$SATQ$, false, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, $SATQ${"questionId":"c5ee6ac0","external_id":"6401adca-8126-4887-bcb0-2e7076d6e999","disclosed_item_id":null,"source":"qbank","vaultid":null,"uId":"929f1f52-65d6-45a4-a78a-c7e4e9d291f8","program":"SAT","test_type":2,"test_type_desc":"Math","primary_class_cd":"Q","domain":"Problem-Solving and Data Analysis","skill_cd":"Q.D.","skill_desc":"Two-variable data: Models and scatterplots","difficulty":"E","score_band_range_cd":2,"type":"mcq","stimulus":null,"stem":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">The scatterplot shows the relationship between two variables, <math alttext=\"x\"><mi>x</mi>\n</math> and <math alttext=\"y\"><mi>y</mi>\n</math>. A line of best fit is also shown.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><figure class='image'><svg height=\"275.22pt\" version=\"1.1\" viewBox=\"0 0 286.56 275.22\" width=\"286.56pt\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"A scatterplot in the x y plane with the origin labeled O. The x axis ranges from 0 to 14 in increments of 2. The y axis ranges from 0 to 20 in increments of 2. Refer to long description.\">\n <defs>\n  <style type=\"text/css\">\n*{stroke-linecap:butt;stroke-linejoin:round;}\n  </style>\n </defs>\n <g id=\"figure_1\">\n  <g id=\"patch_1\">\n   <path d=\"M 0 275.22 \nL 286.56 275.22 \nL 286.56 0 \nL 0 0 \nz\n\" style=\"fill:none;\"></path>\n  </g>\n  <g id=\"axes_1\">\n   <g id=\"patch_2\">\n    <path d=\"M 7.2 260.46 \nL 279.36 260.46 \nL 279.36 10.98 \nL 7.2 10.98 \nz\n\" style=\"fill:none;\"></path>\n   </g>\n   <g id=\"matplotlib.axis_1\"></g>\n   <g id=\"matplotlib.axis_2\"></g>\n  </g>\n  <g id=\"axes_2\">\n   <g id=\"patch_3\">\n    <path d=\"M 9.2008